# Applies to EVERY docker build in this repo, including the existing Flask image
# (root Dockerfile, which does `COPY . .`). So this excludes only artefacts that no
# build ever needs — installed dependencies and build output, all regenerated
# inside the image. Nothing the Flask app reads at runtime is listed here:
# apps/, site-packages/, run.py, gunicorn-cfg.py, log.conf and requirements.txt
# are all still copied.
#
# Without this the build context is ~804 MB; with it, ~344 MB.

# installed dependencies (reinstalled in-image via npm ci / pip install)
**/node_modules
**/.venv
venv

# build output (regenerated by next build / vite build)
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# vcs and local tooling
.git
.github
**/.env.local
**/*.log
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
